00:00:00,010 --> 00:00:05,100
[ Watch on kissFlix.co ]

1
00:00:05,110 --> 00:00:06,528
[♪ tense music playing]

2
00:00:07,195 --> 00:00:08,363
[panting]

3
00:00:08,447 --> 00:00:09,448
[exclaims]

4
00:00:17,831 --> 00:00:18,832
[gasps]

5
00:00:43,649 --> 00:00:44,858
[Kitae] Mr. President.

6
00:00:50,322 --> 00:00:51,323
Uh, sir?

7
00:01:35,659 --> 00:01:36,702
[door slams]

8
00:01:41,623 --> 00:01:42,749
[pants]

9
00:01:42,833 --> 00:01:44,000
Kitae.

10
00:01:51,508 --> 00:01:52,843
-Don't touch me!
-[gasps]

11
00:01:57,931 --> 00:01:59,224
What's going on?

12
00:02:02,811 --> 00:02:03,895
Is he dead?

13
00:02:06,857 --> 00:02:08,066
-Yes.
-[gasps]

14
00:02:10,402 --> 00:02:11,778
It was Cho, wasn't it?

15
00:02:13,655 --> 00:02:14,656
Yeah.

16
00:02:16,783 --> 00:02:18,744
Cho, that lunatic!

17
00:02:18,827 --> 00:02:21,830
[breathing heavily]
I knew he was going to do something.

18
00:02:24,249 --> 00:02:25,834
But to murder the President…

19
00:02:26,835 --> 00:02:27,919
him and Chief Gwak…

20
00:02:36,511 --> 00:02:38,597
[breathing heavily]

21
00:02:44,478 --> 00:02:46,062
What happened to Director Cho?

22
00:03:48,833 --> 00:03:53,755
OCTOBER 27,
MILITARY SECURITY COMMAND

23
00:04:06,685 --> 00:04:09,479
PRESIDENTIAL ASSASSINATION…

24
00:04:12,399 --> 00:04:13,858
[sighs]

25
00:04:19,948 --> 00:04:22,033
Deputy Director, good afternoon.

26
00:04:23,869 --> 00:04:27,247
I've been assigned to this investigation.
I'm Lieutenant Colonel Baek.
STYLE
::cue()

27
00:04:30,166 --> 00:04:33,837
You were at the Gungjeong-dong safe house
after the incident, is that correct?

28
00:04:40,135 --> 00:04:42,554
[slurping]

29
00:04:42,637 --> 00:04:44,139
So why did you show up there?

30
00:04:52,898 --> 00:04:55,692
Your name wasn't
on the guest list for the dinner.

31
00:04:55,775 --> 00:04:57,068
[phone rings]

32
00:04:57,152 --> 00:04:58,904
What time did you arrive last night?

33
00:05:01,281 --> 00:05:02,574
Colonel Ahn Jaeho.

34
00:05:04,576 --> 00:05:05,827
We're beginning the process.

35
00:05:06,870 --> 00:05:08,330
[Kihyun] Who did you come with?

36
00:05:08,413 --> 00:05:10,248
Yes, sir. But, is there…

37
00:05:11,666 --> 00:05:14,002
a specific reason Colonel Baek was, um,

38
00:05:14,085 --> 00:05:15,420
assigned to this post?

39
00:05:17,756 --> 00:05:18,965
Deputy Director,

40
00:05:19,925 --> 00:05:21,718
were you involved
in the President's murder?

41
00:05:29,309 --> 00:05:31,519
If you would prefer to sit here
and remain silent,

42
00:05:32,354 --> 00:05:34,814
we'll assume that you're admitting
to criminal charges.

43
00:05:35,649 --> 00:05:36,691
Is that what you want?

44
00:05:38,234 --> 00:05:41,029
What are you doing? Who made you do this?

45
00:05:49,329 --> 00:05:50,330
Deputy Director…

46
00:05:51,206 --> 00:05:53,249
Look, I think maybe
you're not grasping this…

47
00:05:53,333 --> 00:05:56,962
Your superior shot and killed
the President and you were there!

48
00:06:05,428 --> 00:06:06,930
Ugh, I'm full.

49
00:06:18,566 --> 00:06:19,859
[sighs]

50
00:06:22,362 --> 00:06:23,488
[sighs]

51
00:06:24,489 --> 00:06:25,490
[Kitae clears throat]

52
00:06:26,408 --> 00:06:27,492
Hey, you in there!

53
00:06:28,284 --> 00:06:29,327
Can you hear me?

54
00:06:30,453 --> 00:06:31,538
Listen carefully.

55
00:06:31,621 --> 00:06:34,249
Call up General Jang Mujin.
Do it immediately.

56
00:06:34,749 --> 00:06:36,626
And ask him who captured Director Cho.

57
00:06:37,669 --> 00:06:38,962
All right?

58
00:06:54,561 --> 00:06:56,855
[phone rings]

59
00:06:57,981 --> 00:07:01,526
Baek Kitae is being questioned
by the Joint Investigation Headquarters?

60
00:07:01,609 --> 00:07:04,738
Yes, sir. We heard he was
in Gungjeong-dong that evening.

61
00:07:04,821 --> 00:07:05,905
[Mujin] Yeah, that's right.

62
00:07:05,989 --> 00:07:06,990
…JANG MUJIN

63
00:07:07,073 --> 00:07:08,742
Actually saw him myself at the safe house.

64
00:07:08,825 --> 00:07:09,993
That's why I called you.

65
00:07:10,076 --> 00:07:12,537
We'd just like a chance to
ask some questions, sir.

66
00:07:13,705 --> 00:07:15,457
It won't take long, sir, I promise.

67
00:07:16,249 --> 00:07:18,042
What do you need to question him for?

68
00:07:18,126 --> 00:07:20,211
Colonel Ahn, listen here.

69
00:07:21,463 --> 00:07:22,714
I'm listening, sir.

70
00:07:22,797 --> 00:07:24,591
Release the Deputy Director.

71
00:07:24,674 --> 00:07:26,468
-We can't just let him go without--
-Stop it!

72
00:07:27,010 --> 00:07:28,720
He's the one who captured Director Cho!

73
00:07:29,345 --> 00:07:30,472
What?

74
00:07:30,555 --> 00:07:31,556
If it weren't for him,

75
00:07:31,639 --> 00:07:33,933
this country would be
in Cho's hands right now.

76
00:07:38,897 --> 00:07:40,106
You're telling me…

77
00:07:41,691 --> 00:07:44,486
you really think I was involved
in assassinating the President?

78
00:07:46,279 --> 00:07:49,324
I look like Director Cho to you?
That power-tripping piece of shit.

79
00:07:53,077 --> 00:07:55,121
Get your head straight, Baek Kihyun.

80
00:07:56,247 --> 00:07:58,416
Think carefully about who's on your side.

81
00:07:58,917 --> 00:08:00,043
Who's your friend,

82
00:08:01,377 --> 00:08:03,046
and who's your adversary…

83
00:08:10,261 --> 00:08:11,304
[Kitae sighs]

84
00:08:19,354 --> 00:08:20,772
Deputy Director, sir…

85
00:08:21,773 --> 00:08:23,024
you can leave now.

86
00:08:36,538 --> 00:08:37,539
[Kitae scoffs]

87
00:08:43,086 --> 00:08:44,462
[Jaeho] Let him through.

88
00:08:44,546 --> 00:08:45,630
Sir, what happened?

89
00:08:46,589 --> 00:08:48,383
He was the person
who captured Director Cho.

90
00:08:50,051 --> 00:08:51,052
[sighs]

91
00:08:51,719 --> 00:08:54,305
[♪ inquisitive music playing]
STYLE
::cue()

92
00:08:58,226 --> 00:09:02,147
KOREAN CENTRAL
INTELLIGENCE AGENCY

93
00:09:23,877 --> 00:09:28,089
[Kitae] Sometimes, one split-second
decision changes the course of history.

94
00:09:28,798 --> 00:09:29,966
Sir, wait!

95
00:09:30,633 --> 00:09:31,634
Sir!

96
00:09:31,718 --> 00:09:33,052
-Wait, sir!
-[tires screech]

97
00:09:34,470 --> 00:09:36,264
-What?
-[Kitae] Sir.

98
00:09:36,347 --> 00:09:38,141
Tell me where you're heading.

99
00:09:38,224 --> 00:09:40,643
Well, I'm going to the KCIA.

100
00:09:40,727 --> 00:09:42,562
And what are you planning to do?

101
00:09:42,645 --> 00:09:44,939
Uh… I… I don't know.

102
00:09:45,732 --> 00:09:47,025
[scoffs] Wait a minute.

103
00:09:47,108 --> 00:09:50,236
Hang on.
So all of the gunshots I heard earlier…

104
00:09:50,320 --> 00:09:53,114
Wait… The President is safe, isn't he?

105
00:09:54,324 --> 00:09:56,451
[Kitae] Before assassinating
the President,

106
00:09:56,534 --> 00:09:59,370
Director Cho had summoned
Army Chief of Staff, Jang Mujin,

107
00:09:59,454 --> 00:10:01,456
to the government safe house.

108
00:10:01,539 --> 00:10:05,043
His plan was to take Mujin to KCIA
headquarters after the job was finished,

109
00:10:05,627 --> 00:10:07,921
-and convince him to join his side.
-[breathing shakily]

110
00:10:08,004 --> 00:10:09,172
Mr. Cho, please…

111
00:10:09,714 --> 00:10:11,382
Report to Army headquarters.

112
00:10:12,050 --> 00:10:13,176
Army headquarters?

113
00:10:13,259 --> 00:10:15,178
You'll need the support
of the entire military.

114
00:10:17,472 --> 00:10:19,974
Go to Army headquarters.
Both of you wait there.

115
00:10:20,058 --> 00:10:21,893
I'll take care of everything at the KCIA.

116
00:10:22,977 --> 00:10:24,854
Good plan, we'll drive over now.

117
00:10:24,938 --> 00:10:26,481
You handle the KCIA.

118
00:10:26,564 --> 00:10:28,399
[pants] Don't worry about a thing.

119
00:10:28,483 --> 00:10:30,026
Make sure you get there quickly.

120
00:10:31,527 --> 00:10:33,112
I'll call you ASAP, sir.

121
00:10:33,738 --> 00:10:35,615
[Cho] Let's go! To the Army headquarters!

122
00:10:37,200 --> 00:10:40,161
[Kitae] However, after the deed was done,
Cho started panicking.

123
00:10:41,079 --> 00:10:43,164
-In the end, he decided to trust me…
-[sighs]

124
00:10:43,248 --> 00:10:46,501
…and headed straight to the
Army headquarters instead of the KCIA.

125
00:10:47,627 --> 00:10:49,379
This is KCIA Deputy Director Baek Kitae.

126
00:10:50,129 --> 00:10:51,506
Director Cho killed the President.

127
00:10:51,589 --> 00:10:53,383
He's on his way to Army headquarters now.

128
00:10:54,092 --> 00:10:56,803
As soon as he gets there,
you need to arrest him.

129
00:10:58,137 --> 00:11:00,431
Cho murdered the president,
are you listening?

130
00:11:01,474 --> 00:11:02,725
Arrest him now!

131
00:11:05,520 --> 00:11:07,105
Incompetent son of a bitch.

132
00:11:18,658 --> 00:11:20,618
DEPUTY DIRECTOR BAEK KITAE

133
00:11:22,161 --> 00:11:25,081
[Mujin] You've done an excellent job,
Deputy Director Baek.

134
00:11:25,164 --> 00:11:27,125
-Well done.
-I was just doing my duty.

135
00:11:27,208 --> 00:11:29,752
The KCIA was implicated in this,

136
00:11:29,836 --> 00:11:32,463
so they'll bring in
Joint Investigations for the inquiry.

137
00:11:32,547 --> 00:11:33,798
That concerns me.

138
00:11:34,674 --> 00:11:38,261
A boat that's being rocked
is bound to wind up on the ocean floor.

139
00:11:38,928 --> 00:11:40,013
Yes, of course.

140
00:11:41,222 --> 00:11:43,725
Your concerns make sense,
especially in this climate.

141
00:11:44,350 --> 00:11:45,435
Mr. Baek.

142
00:11:46,227 --> 00:11:47,854
Effective immediately,

143
00:11:47,937 --> 00:11:53,067
I am appointing you acting director
of the Korean Central Intelligence Agency.

144
00:11:55,153 --> 00:11:56,696
I'm very flattered, sir.

145
00:11:56,779 --> 00:11:58,906
Deputy Director… Oh, sorry.

146
00:11:59,824 --> 00:12:01,451
Director Baek, please don't let me down.

147
00:12:02,577 --> 00:12:05,079
Hwang Daesik will take over
unless we act fast.

148
00:12:05,580 --> 00:12:08,499
-That man can't be allowed near power.
-Understood, sir.

149
00:12:09,208 --> 00:12:11,210
[♪ sinister music playing]

150
00:12:21,637 --> 00:12:22,680
[sighs]

151
00:12:34,108 --> 00:12:35,109
PERSONAL DETAILS
BAEK KITAE

152
00:12:35,193 --> 00:12:37,904
Baek Kitae's the one
who captured Director Cho?

153
00:12:37,987 --> 00:12:39,155
Yes, sir.

154
00:12:39,238 --> 00:12:42,575
Cho was headed to the KCIA,
then Baek lured him away.

155
00:12:43,368 --> 00:12:46,079
Ah… That prick.

156
00:12:46,662 --> 00:12:48,039
He's pretty clever.

157
00:12:49,791 --> 00:12:53,336
Guess there's a reason
he was such an asset to the President.

158
00:12:53,878 --> 00:12:55,463
He's acting director now.

159
00:12:56,631 --> 00:12:59,384
He was appointed by
General Jang Mujin this morning.

160
00:12:59,467 --> 00:13:04,263
Okay, so General Jang's
trying to keep us in check. [sighs]

161
00:13:06,307 --> 00:13:08,893
Any other intel
from the guy who brought this?
STYLE
::cue()

162
00:13:08,976 --> 00:13:10,520
-Yes, sir.
-What did he say?

163
00:13:13,773 --> 00:13:16,025
He's going after Chief Cheon's funding.

164
00:13:16,109 --> 00:13:18,194
All the money
he's getting from the government.

165
00:13:18,277 --> 00:13:19,695
[laughs]

166
00:13:22,740 --> 00:13:25,743
That son of a bitch
is pretty clever too, huh?

167
00:13:25,827 --> 00:13:27,036
[Hwang inhales sharply]

168
00:13:27,120 --> 00:13:28,704
He's getting out soon.

169
00:13:29,539 --> 00:13:31,124
At least that's what I've heard.

170
00:13:31,749 --> 00:13:33,167
Yes, speaking of which,

171
00:13:34,419 --> 00:13:36,546
it's about time
he got into the game again.

172
00:13:37,213 --> 00:13:39,090
For real this time. Don't you think?

173
00:13:39,173 --> 00:13:40,174
Agreed.

174
00:13:41,008 --> 00:13:43,386
For real this time. That's right.

175
00:13:43,469 --> 00:13:46,180
Get him a position
in the Joint Investigation Headquarters.

176
00:13:46,264 --> 00:13:47,265
Yes, will do, sir.

177
00:13:47,932 --> 00:13:49,642
[inhales sharply]

178
00:13:49,725 --> 00:13:51,227
Jaeho, listen.

179
00:13:51,310 --> 00:13:52,311
Sir?

180
00:13:52,812 --> 00:13:54,272
You need to realize…

181
00:13:56,649 --> 00:13:59,026
that this assassination is…

182
00:14:00,736 --> 00:14:03,322
nothing less than
an opportunity from heaven.

183
00:14:04,031 --> 00:14:05,908
-[laughs]
-[Jaeho] At this time,

184
00:14:05,992 --> 00:14:09,245
head of Martial Law Joint
Investigation Headquarters, Hwang Daesik

185
00:14:09,328 --> 00:14:12,832
will deliver an interim briefing
on the assassination of the President.

186
00:14:18,754 --> 00:14:21,090
The assassination of the President,

187
00:14:21,174 --> 00:14:23,634
which took place at 7:50 p.m.,

188
00:14:24,385 --> 00:14:28,139
on October 26th in a safe house
in the Gungjeong-dong area,

189
00:14:28,222 --> 00:14:30,808
was tragically committed in a banquet hall

190
00:14:30,892 --> 00:14:34,353
where KCIA officials met
to discuss matters of national security.

191
00:14:35,021 --> 00:14:38,024
This murder was determined
to be premeditated

192
00:14:38,107 --> 00:14:42,111
and carried out by
Mr. Cho Namsik of the KCIA.

193
00:14:43,070 --> 00:14:45,990
The motive was Cho's fear of dismissal.

194
00:14:46,073 --> 00:14:48,242
He had recently lost the president's trust

195
00:14:48,326 --> 00:14:51,787
and was under scrutiny
by the Presidential Security Service.

196
00:14:51,871 --> 00:14:53,831
His ambition was to seize authority,

197
00:14:53,915 --> 00:14:55,833
and become president himself.

198
00:14:55,917 --> 00:15:00,338
His lust for power and control
drove him to commit this monstrous act.

199
00:15:00,963 --> 00:15:02,006
Right now!

200
00:15:03,591 --> 00:15:04,592
Right here!

201
00:15:06,636 --> 00:15:10,973
The KCIA is standing at
the greatest crossroads since inception.

202
00:15:13,684 --> 00:15:16,229
This agency was built with the blood
and sweat of our people

203
00:15:16,312 --> 00:15:18,147
and now we're losing their trust!

204
00:15:19,565 --> 00:15:20,733
Our very name…

205
00:15:21,442 --> 00:15:23,569
Mocked and ridiculed at every turn.

206
00:15:24,820 --> 00:15:26,113
From this day on,

207
00:15:27,240 --> 00:15:29,408
our agency will thrive under my command.

208
00:15:30,868 --> 00:15:32,536
We'll restore our power,

209
00:15:33,454 --> 00:15:36,123
and we will protect
the reputation of the state!

210
00:15:37,124 --> 00:15:39,085
If we want to survive, this is how.

211
00:15:40,169 --> 00:15:43,923
And that will secure
the future of our great nation.

212
00:15:44,799 --> 00:15:49,428
We consider this the greatest tragedy
and most grievous offense

213
00:15:49,512 --> 00:15:51,847
ever committed under the Yushin regime.

214
00:15:52,515 --> 00:15:56,269
In order for us to reestablish
our national security,

215
00:15:56,352 --> 00:16:00,356
all available resources
will be mobilized to prevent recurrence.

216
00:16:01,357 --> 00:16:02,984
We will…

217
00:16:03,067 --> 00:16:04,360
-We will…
-We will…

218
00:16:05,194 --> 00:16:06,654
…work in the shadows!

219
00:16:06,737 --> 00:16:08,614
-…work in the shadows!
-…work in the shadows!

220
00:16:09,532 --> 00:16:10,866
…to defend our sunlit land!

221
00:16:10,950 --> 00:16:13,327
-…to defend our sunlit land!
-…to defend our sunlit land!

222
00:16:14,161 --> 00:16:15,997
-Commander!
-General Hwang, sir!

223
00:16:16,080 --> 00:16:19,834
Do you have anything to say?
Please, just a brief comment, general!

224
00:16:20,334 --> 00:16:23,379
[Kitae] Hwang Daesik, head of
the Joint Investigation Headquarters,

225
00:16:23,462 --> 00:16:26,549
will use his investigative powers
to tear the KCIA apart

226
00:16:26,632 --> 00:16:28,134
and rise to the center of power.

227
00:16:29,468 --> 00:16:31,721
As acting director of the KCIA,

228
00:16:31,804 --> 00:16:34,056
I must find a way
to contain the situation,

229
00:16:34,140 --> 00:16:36,058
stop Hwang from taking over,

230
00:16:36,142 --> 00:16:38,311
and reclaim the KCIA's authority.

231
00:16:38,394 --> 00:16:39,603
That's right.

232
00:16:39,687 --> 00:16:43,232
The KCIA and the JIH
are in a full-blown dogfight.

233
00:16:44,567 --> 00:16:46,360
To our country and its people!

234
00:16:46,444 --> 00:16:47,862
-Here, here!
-Here, here!

235
00:16:51,824 --> 00:16:53,284
[exclaims]

236
00:16:53,367 --> 00:16:55,286
[chanting] Hwang Daesik!

237
00:16:55,369 --> 00:16:58,831
-Hwang Daesik!
-Hwang Daesik!

238
00:16:58,914 --> 00:17:02,710
-Hwang Daesik!
-Hwang Daesik!

239
00:17:02,793 --> 00:17:06,255
-Hwang Daesik!
-Hwang Daesik!

240
00:17:06,339 --> 00:17:13,012
-Hwang Daesik!
-Hwang Daesik!
STYLE
::cue()

241
00:17:18,142 --> 00:17:20,561
The President's dead
and it's time to move forward.

242
00:17:21,687 --> 00:17:23,189
What matters now is…

243
00:17:24,940 --> 00:17:25,941
who comes next.

244
00:17:26,025 --> 00:17:28,903
Who's gonna take his seat
and lead this country?

245
00:17:32,239 --> 00:17:33,658
Who do you think will do it?

246
00:17:35,409 --> 00:17:36,577
Someone once said,

247
00:17:37,745 --> 00:17:41,582
"Kings are only chosen by the heavens."

248
00:17:42,917 --> 00:17:46,212
And I think
you might be heaven's selection.

249
00:17:47,338 --> 00:17:49,131
[chuckles] Come on, what is that?

250
00:18:02,311 --> 00:18:04,063
Hwang's not about to sit and do nothing.

251
00:18:05,398 --> 00:18:07,441
At this point, he's our biggest problem.

252
00:18:07,525 --> 00:18:11,612
That bald, oily son of a bitch.
He just wants status and control.

253
00:18:11,696 --> 00:18:13,864
All of the power and authority

254
00:18:13,948 --> 00:18:16,659
can be found in
the Joint Investigation Headquarters.

255
00:18:17,910 --> 00:18:21,414
Hwang will use the investigation
to eliminate his political enemies.

256
00:18:22,248 --> 00:18:23,582
Ah, shit.

257
00:18:24,583 --> 00:18:28,462
So they'll likely take aim
right at the KCIA from the start.

258
00:18:29,046 --> 00:18:30,339
Exactly.

259
00:18:34,677 --> 00:18:38,806
Which means you and I are both gonna be
on his list of targets to get rid of.

260
00:18:42,309 --> 00:18:44,019
So what's the plan, Baek?

261
00:18:44,103 --> 00:18:47,064
You gonna let it happen?
You gonna just sit there and take it?

262
00:18:55,614 --> 00:18:57,742
[inhales deeply] Well, sir.

263
00:19:01,912 --> 00:19:03,414
Why don't we…

264
00:19:05,040 --> 00:19:07,084
cross the Rubicon together? Join forces.

265
00:19:09,670 --> 00:19:11,672
[♪ tense music playing]

266
00:19:15,301 --> 00:19:16,886
You mean you want us to…

267
00:19:18,304 --> 00:19:19,930
overthrow the government?

268
00:19:22,892 --> 00:19:25,644
You know how this country is structured.
You've seen it,

269
00:19:26,520 --> 00:19:28,397
from the inside, with the President.

270
00:19:36,739 --> 00:19:38,032
[sighs]

271
00:19:45,206 --> 00:19:47,124
[sighs, grunts]

272
00:19:53,339 --> 00:19:55,341
[♪ thrilling music playing]

273
00:20:12,608 --> 00:20:13,859
[sighs] Let's do it.

274
00:20:14,610 --> 00:20:17,029
Yeah. Let's be bold!

275
00:20:17,112 --> 00:20:18,113
-[Kitae applauds]
-[sighs]

276
00:20:22,535 --> 00:20:23,577
First off,

277
00:20:24,286 --> 00:20:26,455
we need to win over
General Jang's support.

278
00:20:26,539 --> 00:20:29,583
Ugh, well he's not exactly
a pushover, is he?

279
00:20:30,417 --> 00:20:32,002
We need the Martial Law Commander
on our side

280
00:20:32,086 --> 00:20:33,504
if we're going to take over the military.

281
00:20:33,587 --> 00:20:34,630
I know.

282
00:20:36,090 --> 00:20:37,633
And we'll get there.

283
00:20:42,346 --> 00:20:44,056
But first, talk to Choi.

284
00:20:44,765 --> 00:20:46,809
Have her bring the money
I entrusted to her.

285
00:20:47,518 --> 00:20:49,645
You ever seen anyone turn down money?

286
00:20:50,521 --> 00:20:51,772
Those Army bastards…

287
00:20:52,481 --> 00:20:54,984
They lose their minds
at the smell of clean cash.

288
00:20:55,568 --> 00:20:57,403
All we have to do is buy them off.

289
00:20:58,696 --> 00:20:59,697
Right. Copy that.

290
00:21:07,496 --> 00:21:08,873
Kitae, look.

291
00:21:11,542 --> 00:21:13,794
I 'm counting on you now, all right?

292
00:21:13,878 --> 00:21:15,004
And you know…

293
00:21:23,345 --> 00:21:25,264
after I move up, you're next.

294
00:21:32,521 --> 00:21:35,608
BUSAN DISTRICT
PROSECUTORS' OFFICE

295
00:21:35,691 --> 00:21:38,402
-[humming]
-[indistinct chattering on TV]

296
00:21:42,865 --> 00:21:46,493
-[reporter] Director Cho announced that…
-[sighs]

297
00:21:46,577 --> 00:21:48,871
-…would mobilize every resource…
-What does this mean?
STYLE
::cue()

298
00:21:48,954 --> 00:21:51,916
…at its disposal
to reestablish national discipline

299
00:21:51,999 --> 00:21:56,921
and prevent any further political violence
or unrest in the coming weeks.

300
00:21:57,004 --> 00:21:59,089
Major General Hwang's promise
to the Korean people

301
00:21:59,173 --> 00:22:01,258
-comes amidst widespread complaints…
-Good morning, ma'am.

302
00:22:01,342 --> 00:22:02,760
…of abuse by the--

303
00:22:03,969 --> 00:22:05,220
Taking a break?

304
00:22:06,138 --> 00:22:07,473
Come on, let's go.

305
00:22:07,556 --> 00:22:09,516
Get back to work. Now!

306
00:22:09,600 --> 00:22:11,477
-Yes, ma'am.
-Let's get back to it.

307
00:22:11,560 --> 00:22:14,104
[sighing, muttering]

308
00:22:15,814 --> 00:22:16,815
[Yejin sighs]

309
00:22:17,691 --> 00:22:19,526
-Kang, over here.
-Yeah, coming.

310
00:22:23,864 --> 00:22:26,408
So Park Changbae,
have you located him yet?

311
00:22:26,492 --> 00:22:30,204
Oh, uh, we're using Kim's statement to
get a general area, then narrow it down,

312
00:22:30,287 --> 00:22:32,706
but he's in Seoul, not Busan,
so it's a bit harder.

313
00:22:33,540 --> 00:22:36,418
Uh, and Ms. Oh,
the chief told us to bury this case.

314
00:22:36,502 --> 00:22:38,963
If he finds out about this,
he's going to blow his top.

315
00:22:39,046 --> 00:22:40,673
-You sure this is okay?
-[phone rings]

316
00:22:40,756 --> 00:22:43,926
-[investigator] Narcotics Unit, Busan…
-[Yejin] All right, Changbae,

317
00:22:44,009 --> 00:22:45,678
-where are you?
-[investigator] She's here. Understood.

318
00:22:46,637 --> 00:22:47,763
Sorry, excuse me, uh…

319
00:22:48,847 --> 00:22:50,724
The chief wants to see you upstairs.

320
00:22:52,059 --> 00:22:53,060
Yes.

321
00:22:53,143 --> 00:22:57,147
[Yejin] "Integrity, honesty, humility."

322
00:22:57,898 --> 00:23:02,528
Wow, Chief. That's a really nice
sentiment for what it's worth.

323
00:23:02,611 --> 00:23:03,988
[Yejin chuckles]

324
00:23:07,241 --> 00:23:08,826
You know, Ms. Oh… [sighs]

325
00:23:08,909 --> 00:23:11,328
…it occurred to me that
even though you've been here a while,

326
00:23:11,412 --> 00:23:15,082
I've never treated you to a cup of tea
in my office, not to mention…

327
00:23:15,165 --> 00:23:18,085
you're the first female prosecutor
in Korean history.

328
00:23:18,168 --> 00:23:19,878
-I should be offering more.
-[chuckles]

329
00:23:20,671 --> 00:23:23,382
Man or woman, male or female,
we're all prosecutors…

330
00:23:23,465 --> 00:23:25,009
We all have the same title.

331
00:23:26,385 --> 00:23:27,428
Hmm…

332
00:23:29,304 --> 00:23:30,723
[both sigh]

333
00:23:31,390 --> 00:23:34,059
So, um,
why am I in the principal's office?

334
00:23:34,643 --> 00:23:35,728
Mmm…

335
00:23:35,811 --> 00:23:37,563
The Joint Investigation Headquarters

336
00:23:37,646 --> 00:23:41,150
is asking us to stop the criminals
who are causing social unrest.

337
00:23:41,233 --> 00:23:42,317
You hear about this?

338
00:23:42,401 --> 00:23:44,111
Yes, sounds familiar.

339
00:23:44,194 --> 00:23:45,446
[inhales sharply] Although, I don't…

340
00:23:46,905 --> 00:23:50,409
I don't know why it'd be their purview
to look into something like that, do you?

341
00:23:50,492 --> 00:23:52,369
Well, they'd probably say something like,

342
00:23:52,453 --> 00:23:54,747
"We are in an unprecedented
time of crisis,

343
00:23:54,830 --> 00:23:56,623
so if we want to prevent further unrest,

344
00:23:56,707 --> 00:23:59,877
prosecutors should expand
the scope of their job

345
00:23:59,960 --> 00:24:01,211
as a duty to the country."

346
00:24:02,671 --> 00:24:05,758
Anyway, on that note,
remember that narcotics case you had?

347
00:24:06,884 --> 00:24:09,011
The one that's been shut down for a while…

348
00:24:09,678 --> 00:24:11,680
You wanna maybe reopen it?

349
00:24:18,187 --> 00:24:19,396
All of a sudden?

350
00:24:20,439 --> 00:24:22,775
Why? Why reopen it?

351
00:24:22,858 --> 00:24:24,860
Well, it was your case originally, right?

352
00:24:24,943 --> 00:24:27,237
Yeah, sure. It was, but still, sir…

353
00:24:30,407 --> 00:24:34,912
Was this an order you got
from a director way up the flagpole?

354
00:24:34,995 --> 00:24:36,663
What are you talking about, Ms. Oh?

355
00:24:36,747 --> 00:24:39,416
We're supposed to be
prosecuting drug crimes, regardless.

356
00:24:40,375 --> 00:24:43,712
And if we're gonna do it,
might as well go for broke.

357
00:24:43,796 --> 00:24:47,216
We'll support with every resource
our office can give.

358
00:24:47,716 --> 00:24:49,301
Do you mean that, sir?

359
00:24:50,803 --> 00:24:52,054
Please don't be generous

360
00:24:52,137 --> 00:24:54,389
if you're gonna go back on your word
and break your promise.

361
00:24:54,473 --> 00:24:56,433
Hey. Have I ever done that, Ms. Oh?

362
00:24:56,517 --> 00:24:57,935
Yes, many times.

363
00:24:58,018 --> 00:24:59,436
[sighs]

364
00:24:59,520 --> 00:25:01,605
I'm serious in this case.

365
00:25:01,688 --> 00:25:04,149
The people at Joint Investigations
need a prosecutor,

366
00:25:04,233 --> 00:25:05,984
and they specifically requested you.

367
00:25:06,068 --> 00:25:07,361
Is that a joke?

368
00:25:07,444 --> 00:25:08,445
No.

369
00:25:08,529 --> 00:25:09,905
Why me though?

370
00:25:09,988 --> 00:25:11,448
How should I know?

371
00:25:12,658 --> 00:25:14,535
But… Mmm…

372
00:25:14,618 --> 00:25:18,413
You happen to know someone there?
Over at the JIH?

373
00:25:19,957 --> 00:25:21,125
Not at all.

374
00:25:38,100 --> 00:25:40,602
[gasps] Whoa.

375
00:26:02,833 --> 00:26:05,294
JOINT INVESTIGATION HEADQUARTERS
INVESTIGATION DIVISION

376
00:26:05,377 --> 00:26:06,461
[clears throat]

377
00:26:11,175 --> 00:26:14,011
[Jaeho] Investigate thoroughly
and tell your men to keep security tight.

378
00:26:14,094 --> 00:26:15,929
-Understood?
-[soldiers] Yes, sir.
STYLE
::cue()

379
00:26:20,601 --> 00:26:21,977
Prosecutor Oh Yejin?

380
00:26:24,313 --> 00:26:26,356
I'm Colonel Ahn,
Chief of Security Department.

381
00:26:27,649 --> 00:26:28,650
Oh Yejin, nice to meet you.

382
00:26:29,818 --> 00:26:31,153
This way.

383
00:26:53,258 --> 00:26:54,760
You can wait here, Ms. Oh.

384
00:26:56,720 --> 00:26:58,096
Ah, also…

385
00:26:59,556 --> 00:27:01,850
I've heard positive things
from the advisor.

386
00:27:01,934 --> 00:27:03,101
I'm excited to work with you.

387
00:27:03,894 --> 00:27:05,062
The advisor?

388
00:27:05,145 --> 00:27:06,521
He'll be here in a moment.

389
00:27:09,775 --> 00:27:11,026
The advisor?

390
00:27:12,903 --> 00:27:14,196
[sighs]

391
00:27:14,279 --> 00:27:16,657
Geez, could they make it
any darker in here?

392
00:27:16,740 --> 00:27:18,200
Looks like a damn crypt.

393
00:27:40,973 --> 00:27:42,975
SPECIAL ADVISOR JANG GEONYOUNG

394
00:27:55,362 --> 00:27:58,365
Congratulations
on the promotion, Director.

395
00:27:58,448 --> 00:27:59,992
So, what are you doing in Seoul?

396
00:28:01,034 --> 00:28:03,704
Well, they transferred me
as deputy director.

397
00:28:05,914 --> 00:28:08,417
They promoted you,
so your old job opened up.

398
00:28:11,378 --> 00:28:13,005
I'm your replacement.

399
00:28:13,088 --> 00:28:16,717
You're number one, and I'm number two.

400
00:28:18,468 --> 00:28:19,469
Hang on.

401
00:28:21,555 --> 00:28:23,390
Chief Cheon didn't tell you, did he?

402
00:28:23,890 --> 00:28:27,144
[chuckles] Sorry.
I just assumed you already knew.

403
00:28:29,521 --> 00:28:31,356
He really didn't discuss it with you
at all?

404
00:28:32,941 --> 00:28:34,651
Wow. Man.

405
00:28:35,277 --> 00:28:37,487
That's not right.
He screwed up on that one.

406
00:28:39,031 --> 00:28:40,032
[sighs]

407
00:28:41,533 --> 00:28:42,743
It's a big office.

408
00:28:46,788 --> 00:28:49,583
Well, I'm sure he had his reasons
for bringing you in.

409
00:28:51,460 --> 00:28:54,254
So do your job well.
And stay out of trouble.

410
00:28:55,005 --> 00:28:56,465
Yes, sir. Director.

411
00:28:57,507 --> 00:28:59,760
Oh, by the way,
I heard you got interrogated.

412
00:29:02,971 --> 00:29:05,307
Hauled you
into Joint Investigation Headquarters.

413
00:29:05,390 --> 00:29:07,392
Sounds like
General Hwang's out to get you.

414
00:29:07,893 --> 00:29:09,686
Know what people have
been calling him lately?

415
00:29:09,770 --> 00:29:11,313
The Bald Rhino.

416
00:29:11,396 --> 00:29:12,898
Correct! [chuckles]

417
00:29:12,981 --> 00:29:17,027
He's so determined that he'll bulldoze
over everything in his way

418
00:29:17,110 --> 00:29:18,403
to get what he wants.

419
00:29:18,487 --> 00:29:22,532
He throws all his weight at the problem
and rams ahead until he reaches his goal.

420
00:29:23,116 --> 00:29:24,826
He's bald, too, so yeah.

421
00:29:24,910 --> 00:29:27,162
Lot of bald guys are like that.

422
00:29:27,245 --> 00:29:28,872
But honestly, here's the problem.

423
00:29:30,874 --> 00:29:33,126
The agency's rep has
been pretty bad lately.

424
00:29:33,752 --> 00:29:35,587
You really think we can win against Hwang?

425
00:29:37,547 --> 00:29:38,924
What do you think, sir?

426
00:29:55,690 --> 00:29:56,691
Hmm?

427
00:30:16,670 --> 00:30:18,505
Want me to send you back to Busan?

428
00:30:19,089 --> 00:30:21,883
'Cause it's starting to feel like
you're here to antagonize me.

429
00:30:22,759 --> 00:30:23,760
Well?

430
00:30:25,095 --> 00:30:26,179
Hey.

431
00:30:27,305 --> 00:30:28,306
Pyo Haksu.

432
00:30:29,766 --> 00:30:31,309
You bald little rat.

433
00:30:36,106 --> 00:30:37,482
Yes, Kitae?

434
00:30:37,566 --> 00:30:39,109
"Yes, sir."

435
00:30:40,193 --> 00:30:41,528
Sir, I'm sorry.

436
00:30:42,904 --> 00:30:44,489
You better get it together.

437
00:30:46,449 --> 00:30:48,160
Understood, I'm very sorry.
STYLE
::cue()

438
00:30:49,035 --> 00:30:51,538
CHIEF OF SECURITY DEPARTMENT
AHN JAEHO

439
00:30:53,081 --> 00:30:55,125
-Ah, you're here.
-Oh. Let me get that, sir.

440
00:30:55,208 --> 00:30:56,334
Oh, yeah, thanks.

441
00:30:58,795 --> 00:31:00,088
-What's this box for?
-[door closes]

442
00:31:00,797 --> 00:31:01,798
Oh, that?

443
00:31:02,591 --> 00:31:04,092
Ah, well,

444
00:31:04,676 --> 00:31:07,596
Chief Cheon's slush fund,
we're keeping a paper trail on it.

445
00:31:09,598 --> 00:31:10,849
You want the assignment?

446
00:31:12,684 --> 00:31:14,352
Is there some reason you're choosing me?

447
00:31:15,395 --> 00:31:17,731
Well, you're…
you're the smartest one here.

448
00:31:19,149 --> 00:31:20,150
It's true.

449
00:31:23,195 --> 00:31:26,031
Special orders from the commander,
so be diligent, all right?

450
00:31:26,615 --> 00:31:29,409
Go through these, figure out
the full extent of the slush fund

451
00:31:29,492 --> 00:31:30,702
and report back.

452
00:31:32,996 --> 00:31:34,247
Yes, sir. Of course.

453
00:31:37,375 --> 00:31:38,376
[door opens]

454
00:32:08,073 --> 00:32:09,074
MILITARY SECURITY COMMAND

455
00:32:09,157 --> 00:32:10,784
PERSONAL RECORD - 1. PERSONAL
DETAILS - NAME: BAEK KITAE

456
00:32:15,664 --> 00:32:19,876
9 YEARS EARLIER, BUSAN

457
00:32:20,502 --> 00:32:22,545
I heard you joined Security Command.

458
00:32:24,130 --> 00:32:26,174
Tell me why you asked to see me, sir.

459
00:32:29,678 --> 00:32:32,097
What did Jang Geonyoung say
when he visited you?

460
00:32:35,308 --> 00:32:37,769
Did you see me in Saigon? See what I did?

461
00:32:39,771 --> 00:32:40,772
Yes, I remember.

462
00:32:41,356 --> 00:32:44,401
So what are you going to do now?
Try to take me down?

463
00:32:47,570 --> 00:32:48,697
Look, Kihyun.

464
00:32:49,322 --> 00:32:50,699
You need to choose.

465
00:32:54,744 --> 00:32:56,454
If I did come after you,

466
00:32:58,415 --> 00:33:00,000
what would you do about it?

467
00:33:03,878 --> 00:33:05,755
Well, if it weren't for me,

468
00:33:07,299 --> 00:33:09,175
you think you'd be where you are now?

469
00:33:12,345 --> 00:33:13,346
What?

470
00:33:13,847 --> 00:33:15,348
Am I wrong here?

471
00:33:17,892 --> 00:33:19,311
You threatening me?

472
00:33:22,772 --> 00:33:26,276
I won't consider you family
if you decide to get aggressive with this.

473
00:33:27,152 --> 00:33:29,279
Either you go down, or I do.

474
00:33:30,613 --> 00:33:31,906
Or maybe we both will.

475
00:33:34,117 --> 00:33:35,869
So I would think of your family

476
00:33:36,953 --> 00:33:39,706
when you're choosing
which route to take here.

477
00:33:42,625 --> 00:33:44,085
Just like I did

478
00:33:46,296 --> 00:33:47,505
for Soyeong

479
00:33:49,007 --> 00:33:50,091
and for you.

480
00:34:07,567 --> 00:34:08,693
[sighs]

481
00:34:09,486 --> 00:34:11,488
[♪ classical music playing]

482
00:34:28,463 --> 00:34:29,964
Who was it anyway?
STYLE
::cue()

483
00:34:30,673 --> 00:34:33,093
Who exactly ordered my interrogation?

484
00:34:33,843 --> 00:34:35,845
Colonel Ahn gave the assignment.

485
00:34:36,721 --> 00:34:37,722
[scoffs]

486
00:34:38,932 --> 00:34:40,517
So he put you to the test

487
00:34:41,476 --> 00:34:43,228
to see how you'd react.

488
00:34:48,983 --> 00:34:50,568
Any other information?

489
00:34:52,779 --> 00:34:54,364
He hasn't said very much.

490
00:34:57,158 --> 00:35:00,870
They'll keep pressuring you,
the Joint Investigation Headquarters.

491
00:35:02,831 --> 00:35:04,332
Know what I mean, Kihyun?

492
00:35:09,587 --> 00:35:10,714
Oh, by the way,

493
00:35:10,797 --> 00:35:12,674
there's something I need you to do.

494
00:35:14,342 --> 00:35:17,762
Keep close tabs on what happens
at the JIH and report back to me.

495
00:35:17,846 --> 00:35:19,931
So I'm supposed to act as your mole now?

496
00:35:20,682 --> 00:35:22,392
The fact is we're at war.

497
00:35:23,184 --> 00:35:25,145
And it won't end until one side falls.

498
00:35:25,228 --> 00:35:30,734
Our whole family will go down
if I'm the one who falls.

499
00:35:45,248 --> 00:35:47,333
It's amazing how you always do this.

500
00:35:50,044 --> 00:35:52,464
You can't hold our family captive forever.

501
00:35:57,594 --> 00:35:58,762
Are you saying

502
00:36:00,138 --> 00:36:01,890
you want to go against me?

503
00:36:30,627 --> 00:36:32,128
[thudding]

504
00:36:35,173 --> 00:36:36,174
[phone ringing]

505
00:36:52,690 --> 00:36:53,942
I've got the money ready.

506
00:36:54,651 --> 00:36:56,152
How long 'til it gets here?

507
00:36:56,236 --> 00:36:58,321
Around two days. I'm gonna bring it.

508
00:36:58,404 --> 00:36:59,989
You mean you personally?

509
00:37:00,073 --> 00:37:02,492
Of course. It's a hefty sum.

510
00:37:02,575 --> 00:37:04,619
Besides, we have some things to discuss.

511
00:37:04,702 --> 00:37:06,329
Really? Like what?

512
00:37:09,207 --> 00:37:12,335
Well, martial law's putting quite a dent
in our sales.

513
00:37:12,418 --> 00:37:13,753
So we better strategize.

514
00:37:15,839 --> 00:37:17,966
All right, then. I'll be waiting for you.

515
00:37:42,156 --> 00:37:43,575
-Morning, sir!
-[door closes]

516
00:37:50,707 --> 00:37:51,916
What, Captain Min?

517
00:37:52,625 --> 00:37:55,795
Oh. You're needed
at Joint Investigation Headquarters.

518
00:37:55,879 --> 00:37:58,506
-The Colonel requested your presence.
-Really?

519
00:37:58,590 --> 00:37:59,591
Yes, sir.

520
00:38:11,227 --> 00:38:12,478
Is there something else?
STYLE
::cue()

521
00:38:13,146 --> 00:38:14,230
Uh…

522
00:38:14,981 --> 00:38:18,318
Rumor is they've been planning
to increase their personnel.

523
00:38:19,068 --> 00:38:20,069
And?

524
00:38:21,362 --> 00:38:22,780
Would you recommend me?

525
00:38:29,162 --> 00:38:31,998
I heard about you
from the Busan Prosecutors' Office.

526
00:38:32,081 --> 00:38:33,666
You're kinda famous over there.

527
00:38:34,417 --> 00:38:36,502
Nah, that's really not true.

528
00:38:36,586 --> 00:38:40,381
I keep the wheels turning, that's all.
Just try to keep the place on track.

529
00:38:40,465 --> 00:38:42,008
-Smooth things over.
-Mm-hmm.

530
00:38:42,091 --> 00:38:43,426
Well, that's not what I heard.

531
00:38:44,052 --> 00:38:46,179
-There are some colorful stories.
-[chuckles]

532
00:38:47,096 --> 00:38:48,097
Oh, really?

533
00:38:48,640 --> 00:38:50,141
They say I'm outta my goddamn mind?

534
00:38:50,224 --> 00:38:51,684
[laughs]

535
00:38:51,768 --> 00:38:53,019
-[coughing]
-Hear that?

536
00:38:53,102 --> 00:38:54,437
[laughing]

537
00:38:54,520 --> 00:38:55,688
That funny to you?

538
00:38:55,772 --> 00:38:58,524
-Uh, no. It's, uh, not funny at all.
-[investigator] Hey, hand me that stapler.

539
00:38:58,608 --> 00:38:59,692
[Jaeho] No, no, sorry, uh…

540
00:39:00,526 --> 00:39:02,278
No one said you're crazy really.

541
00:39:03,029 --> 00:39:04,989
More like prone to impulsivity, reckless.

542
00:39:05,073 --> 00:39:06,699
Look, I have self-control.

543
00:39:07,951 --> 00:39:09,744
I just don't like to bother with it.

544
00:39:09,827 --> 00:39:13,373
Am I supposed to be a hall monitor
or am I supposed to bust criminals?

545
00:39:13,456 --> 00:39:15,458
-Who cares how I do it?
-Just like I heard.

546
00:39:15,541 --> 00:39:17,043
You've got a big pair of balls on you.

547
00:39:37,313 --> 00:39:38,439
Ah. There he is.

548
00:39:40,191 --> 00:39:41,359
Oh, Colonel Baek!

549
00:39:45,488 --> 00:39:46,656
Say hello.

550
00:39:46,739 --> 00:39:49,075
She works
in the Busan District Prosecutors' Office.

551
00:39:49,158 --> 00:39:50,159
Oh Yejin. It's a pleasure.

552
00:39:51,035 --> 00:39:52,120
Baek Kihyun, ma'am.

553
00:39:52,745 --> 00:39:54,789
Nice to meet you. How's your sister?

554
00:39:56,874 --> 00:39:59,210
You know her? You two met?

555
00:39:59,293 --> 00:40:01,212
Yeah, in Busan, I knew her…

556
00:40:01,295 --> 00:40:04,257
[chuckles] …not super well,
just a little bit.

557
00:40:05,008 --> 00:40:06,009
I see.

558
00:40:06,092 --> 00:40:07,719
[Kang] Yeah, all right.

559
00:40:08,761 --> 00:40:11,264
Okay, Ms. Oh, everything's ready.
We should head out now.

560
00:40:11,889 --> 00:40:13,850
Uh-huh. Let's move then.

561
00:40:13,933 --> 00:40:15,309
See you around, Mr. Baek.

562
00:40:16,394 --> 00:40:17,395
All right, move it!

563
00:40:17,478 --> 00:40:18,604
-Okay.
-Yes, ma'am.

564
00:40:20,273 --> 00:40:22,275
-[investigator] Goodbye.
-[Kang] Hey, grab the radios.

565
00:40:22,358 --> 00:40:24,527
This way. There's someone you should meet.

566
00:40:31,451 --> 00:40:32,618
Close the door.

567
00:40:33,786 --> 00:40:34,787
Have a seat.

568
00:40:37,498 --> 00:40:39,125
So who am I meeting?

569
00:40:39,208 --> 00:40:40,877
Well actually, you know him already.

570
00:40:43,755 --> 00:40:47,258
He'll be here soon.
So let's have a smoke while we're waiting.

571
00:40:47,341 --> 00:40:48,384
Sure.

572
00:40:56,434 --> 00:40:57,560
[lighter ignites]

573
00:41:08,279 --> 00:41:09,322
Let's see.

574
00:41:09,405 --> 00:41:11,365
All right. We've got a few minutes.

575
00:41:30,551 --> 00:41:31,761
-Sir.
-Thanks.

576
00:41:32,637 --> 00:41:33,679
Here.

577
00:41:40,937 --> 00:41:43,314
The raw materials are coming today,
you're sure?

578
00:41:43,397 --> 00:41:44,607
Yes, I'm sure.
STYLE
::cue()

579
00:41:53,908 --> 00:41:55,660
[Haksu] I heard you're going to Busan.

580
00:41:56,911 --> 00:41:58,287
Why make the trip, sir?

581
00:41:59,372 --> 00:42:00,581
I've got some business.

582
00:42:01,124 --> 00:42:02,500
What kind?

583
00:42:05,336 --> 00:42:07,380
Do I have to tell you everything?

584
00:42:08,881 --> 00:42:10,466
Just making conversation.

585
00:42:11,717 --> 00:42:13,678
-[knocks on door]
-[door opens]

586
00:42:21,018 --> 00:42:23,688
Director, the car is ready for you.

587
00:42:23,771 --> 00:42:25,231
Okay.

588
00:42:25,815 --> 00:42:26,816
You're going along?

589
00:42:29,694 --> 00:42:30,695
Yes.

590
00:42:34,532 --> 00:42:36,784
You never even called
once you moved to Seoul.

591
00:42:37,368 --> 00:42:39,620
I apologize.
I've been getting settled in Seoul.

592
00:42:39,704 --> 00:42:41,247
-I'm busy.
-You goddamn little shit.

593
00:42:42,415 --> 00:42:44,876
-Sir?
-What's with your tone?

594
00:42:44,959 --> 00:42:46,711
What about my tone?

595
00:42:46,794 --> 00:42:48,129
-Hey!
-You…

596
00:42:52,758 --> 00:42:54,010
The hell are you doing?

597
00:42:59,974 --> 00:43:01,934
Do what I told you. I expect some results.

598
00:43:02,894 --> 00:43:03,895
Yes, Mr. Baek, sir.

599
00:43:04,812 --> 00:43:06,564
-Let's go.
-I'll see you when you're back.

600
00:43:09,942 --> 00:43:11,110
[door opens]

601
00:43:19,702 --> 00:43:21,120
[in English] Boys,

602
00:43:22,914 --> 00:43:24,290
be ambitious!

603
00:43:49,774 --> 00:43:51,317
[line ringing]

604
00:43:55,154 --> 00:43:56,530
It's Haksu. Hello.

605
00:43:58,532 --> 00:44:01,244
1:08 A.M., BUSAN

606
00:44:44,370 --> 00:44:45,496
Okay. They're on the move.

607
00:44:45,579 --> 00:44:50,251
1:15 A.M., SEOUL

608
00:44:51,168 --> 00:44:53,713
Ms. Oh. They just arrived.

609
00:44:54,922 --> 00:44:57,591
[shutters clicking]

610
00:45:22,325 --> 00:45:26,620
BAEKHO TRADING INC.

611
00:45:27,663 --> 00:45:29,665
[shutters continue clicking]

612
00:45:35,713 --> 00:45:40,009
1:38 A.M., BUSAN

613
00:45:45,222 --> 00:45:46,640
What's your plan now?

614
00:45:48,934 --> 00:45:50,936
What's all this money going to be for?

615
00:45:52,146 --> 00:45:53,314
Patriotism.

616
00:46:01,197 --> 00:46:03,949
How? With a showdown?
You gonna start some kind of gunfight?

617
00:46:05,743 --> 00:46:07,370
Well, I've come this far.

618
00:46:08,204 --> 00:46:09,413
Can't stop now.

619
00:46:13,084 --> 00:46:14,543
Are you sure you can pull it off?

620
00:46:15,503 --> 00:46:17,254
Honestly, I'm not sure that matters.

621
00:46:20,049 --> 00:46:21,842
All that matters in a gunfight is

622
00:46:23,469 --> 00:46:25,179
who's faster on the draw.

623
00:46:32,478 --> 00:46:33,604
[soldier] Open fire!

624
00:46:35,314 --> 00:46:36,440
Get down!

625
00:47:29,368 --> 00:47:30,369
Long time no see.

